# bron-resins catalog -- every resin named, and every resin's bytes sealed SHA3-256.
#
# THE PROMISE THIS FILE KEEPS. `foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md` states the
# cellar's own clause: *every resin records the marks of what it seals, so a reader in another
# decade knows what the cellar held without opening it.* One `entry` line per resin says what the
# cellar holds, and one `seal` line says its bytes are the bytes. The same page names all three
# fields a manifest line carries -- *its type-mark, its digest at the tiers the resins law fixes,
# and its name* -- and the vow beneath them: *the digest is checked twice*.
#
# REFRESHED `20260906.233111`, after a measurement. The habit was kept for the first three files
# of the first morning and dropped: the room held 17 resins and this catalog named 3, and nothing
# in the tree read it -- three scans name `bron-resins/` only to skip it as testimony. A catalog
# covering a fifth of its room reads exactly like a whole one. Fourteen entries were written from
# each resin's OWN first header line rather than from a summary, and the catalog now has a reader:
# `tools/b/bron_resins_catalog_witness.rish` holds uncatalogued, orphaned, and duplicated lines at
# zero on every lap, so this file can never quietly go stale again.
#
# SEALED `20260910.014500`, which is the field that refresh still lacked. Names and notes had grown
# whole while the digest the law names stayed absent, so a resin edited in place would have passed
# every reading above in silence. Each `seal` line records SHA3-256 computed by
# `crypto/sha3_digest.rye` over authored Keccak, so checking one needs this tree and no external
# binary. The catalog seals every resin and never itself -- a file cannot carry its own digest, and
# the catalog's own bytes ride in the git history each seal travels in.
#
# WHAT THE SEVENTEEN DIGESTS ARE, measured rather than assumed. Every resin in this room has
# exactly one commit in the tree's whole history, and its blob at that commit is byte-identical to
# its blob at HEAD -- checked one file at a time, all seventeen equal. So each seal below is the
# seal of the bytes that LANDED, rather than of bytes that merely stand here today.
format bron-resins-v1
stamp 20260712.115753
refreshed 20260906.233111
purpose chat-printout essay resins as Bron values at the seam
law Bron carries immutable values; Brix composes wholes; this folder holds Bron only
witness tools/b/bron_resins_catalog_witness.rish -- uncatalogued, orphan, duplicate, unsealed, and mismatched lines at zero
entry 20260712-115753_morning-fold-thoughts.bron fuller morning summary and Rio essay as chat-printout-v1
